.TH CF-DNS 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-dns.1 \- Manage DNS records, BIND import, and export
.PP
Manage DNS records for your Cloudflare zones, including record creation, bulk queries, proxy toggling, and BIND zone file import/export.
.PP
.PP
.SH REQUIRED PERMISSIONS
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
Read
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.DNS:Read\fR
.TP
Write
\fIMinimum Cloudflare API Token Scope:\fR \fBZone.DNS:Edit\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS OVERVIEW
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns list\fR (#cf-dns-list) — List DNS records with optional filtering
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns get\fR (#cf-dns-get) — Retrieve specific DNS record details
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns create\fR (#cf-dns-create) — Add a new DNS record
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns update\fR (#cf-dns-update) — Full update of an existing record (PUT)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns patch\fR (#cf-dns-patch) — Partial update of specific fields (PATCH)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns delete\fR (#cf-dns-delete) — Remove a DNS record
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns import\fR (#cf-dns-import) — Import records from a standard BIND zone file
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf dns export\fR (#cf-dns-export) — Export zone records in BIND zone file format
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns list\fR"
.PP
Lists all DNS records for a given zone.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns list --zone <zone-id-or-name> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--zone <id-or-name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Target Zone ID or domain name
.TP
\fB--type <type>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Filter by DNS type (\fBA\fR, \fBAAAA\fR, \fBCNAME\fR, \fBTXT\fR, \fBMX\fR, etc.)
.TP
\fB--name <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Filter by exact record hostname
.TP
\fB--content <content>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Filter by IP address or record content
.TP
\fB--page <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR \fB1\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Page number
.TP
\fB--per-page <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR \fB20\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Results per page
.TP
\fB--all\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDefault:\fR \fBfalse\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Fetch all records across all pages
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# List all records for a zone
cf dns list --zone example.com

# Filter to show only MX records
cf dns list --zone example.com --type MX

# Find all records pointing to a specific origin server IP
cf dns list --zone example.com --content 198.51.100.1
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns get\fR"
.PP
Retrieve full details for a single DNS record by its ID.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns get --zone <zone-id-or-name> --id <record-id>
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns get --zone example.com --id 372e67954025e0ba6aaa6d586b9e0b59
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns create\fR"
.PP
Creates a new DNS record in your zone.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns create --zone <zone> --type <type> --name <name> --content <content> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--zone <id-or-name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Zone ID or domain name
.TP
\fB--type <type>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Record type (\fBA\fR, \fBAAAA\fR, \fBCNAME\fR, \fBTXT\fR, \fBMX\fR, \fBSRV\fR, etc.)
.TP
\fB--name <name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Subdomain or \fB@\fR for root domain
.TP
\fB--content <content>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR \fIrequired\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Target IP, hostname, or text value
.TP
\fB--ttl <seconds>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR \fB1\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Time To Live in seconds (\fB1\fR for Automatic)
.TP
\fB--proxied\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDefault:\fR \fBfalse\fR | \fIDescription:\fR Enable Cloudflare proxy (CDN, DDoS protection, WAF)
.TP
\fB--priority <num>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Priority for \fBMX\fR and \fBSRV\fR records
.TP
\fB--comment <text>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDefault:\fR  | \fIDescription:\fR Optional administrative comment
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Create a proxied root A record
cf dns create --zone example.com --type A --name @ --content 203.0.113.195 --proxied

# Create an unproxied CNAME with 300s TTL
cf dns create --zone example.com --type CNAME --name mail --content mail.provider.net --ttl 300

# Create an MX record with priority 10
cf dns create --zone example.com --type MX --name @ --content mail.example.com --priority 10
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns patch\fR"
.PP
Partially updates an existing DNS record without needing to re-specify all original fields.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns patch --zone <zone> --id <record-id> [fields...]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--zone <id-or-name>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Zone ID or domain name
.TP
\fB--id <record-id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Target record ID
.TP
\fB--content <content>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR New record target IP or value
.TP
\fB--proxied\fR
\fIType:\fR boolean | \fIDescription:\fR Update proxy status (\fB--proxied\fR or \fB--no-proxied\fR)
.TP
\fB--ttl <seconds>\fR
\fIType:\fR number | \fIDescription:\fR Update TTL in seconds
.TP
\fB--comment <text>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Update comment
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Toggle proxy status without changing the IP
cf dns patch --zone example.com --id <record-id> --proxied

# Update the target IP only
cf dns patch --zone example.com --id <record-id> --content 198.51.100.20
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns delete\fR"
.PP
Removes a DNS record.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns delete --zone <zone> --id <record-id> [--yes]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf dns delete --zone example.com --id 372e67954025e0ba6aaa6d586b9e0b59 --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf dns import\fR & \fBcf dns export\fR"
.PP
Backup and migrate DNS configurations using standard BIND format files.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Export all records to standard BIND zone file format
cf dns export --zone example.com > example.com.zone

# Import records from a BIND zone file (with optional proxy toggle)
cf dns import --zone example.com --file example.com.zone [--proxied]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
